c(1, "header lines 1-6; §2.1; §2.1 table (verbatim); §2.2 table (verbatim); §2.5", "positioning", "Quit Bad Habits & Addiction — Sobriety Counter & Tracker (App Store ID 1658588991, com.shpavda.bad-habit-break; in-app 'Bad Habit Break'; RU store name 'Без вредных привычек: дни') by SHPAVDA, TOO (© Aliaksei Shpauda), released 2023-01-17, current 1.2.2 (2026-07-30), RU Lifestyle chart 'номер 45', Free with advertising and two ad-removal subscriptions (Monthly $0.99 / Yearly $9.99; RU 99 ₽ / 699 ₽), store language field English only though the description claims 70+ languages, age 9+ — a sobriety/abstinence counter: any number of bad habits, time since quitting to the second, a current goal that steps up automatically (1, 7, 30 days, a month, 100 years), a personal record, an attempts counter, a relapse button that resets the timer and stores a note with reason and date, a tree logo inside a filling circle, articles, a colour per habit, dark theme; per reviewers no notifications, no widget, no account, no goal editing; version history: 1.1.1 'Added subscriptions' (2023-04), 17 languages (2023-06), then none for 19 months, 1.2.0 'translated into more languages' (2026-07-15), 1.2.1 'Improved application performance' (2026-07-21), 1.2.2 (2026-07-30); the same developer ships a good-habits app hit by the same crash. Feature table (verbatim): " + table("## 2.1 What the product is", 0) + " || listing (verbatim): " + table("## 2.2 What the store listing says", 0) + " — not establishable: downloads, conversion, revenue, refunds, churn; when ads were introduced or changed; whether the paywall screens reviewers describe exist or are ad-removal offers read as a paywall; what the goal ladder is and whether custom goals were removed; which ad networks and categories are served; what caused the July 2026 crash beyond reviewer reports.", "free counter, ads, ad-removal subscription only", "praise", "614 reviews, 37 storefronts, 14 languages, 2023-01-31 → 2026-09-06, mean 4.397★; 79 codes; 101 checks; 26 absence tests", "none", "header", "app-specific", ["10508150052", "9568198570", "11090976286", "14274384633"], "", "a free Russian-market sobriety counter whose one paid item is ad removal")

c(2, "How to read this; Nine warnings 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 9; §1.1 table (verbatim); §1.2 table (verbatim); §1.3 table (verbatim); §1.4; §1.5 table (verbatim); §1.6", "data-caveat", "Method and limits: every one of 614 reviews read in date order in the original language (Russian 516, English 42, Ukrainian 15, Spanish 12, German 5, Turkish and Portuguese 4, Polish and Vietnamese 3, Japanese 2, Norwegian/Italian/French/Arabic 1, two emoji-only, two with letters but no language), 79 codes in 12 families (76 hand, 3 mechanical), 22 unions plus U:negative_any, 101 checks (57 forward text-to-code ties, 18 reverse vocabulary tests; first run failed 18, 2 real errors), 26 absence tests; no duplicates, no repeat authors, no edited review; only Russia (407) and the US (56) reach 50 — together 75.41% — and 17 storefronts hold one review; a Russian-language corpus (84.04%, including 41 of 56 US-storefront reviews — 'the US findings describe mostly Russian speakers using US App Store accounts'); no version field and one-line release notes — timing, not proven cause, though 21 reviewers themselves say the crash began after the update; 281 reviews (45.77%) under 60 characters; helpful votes rare (55) and concentrated (the three most-voted, 109/33/32, all ask for tree growth or a widget); PAID_EXPLICIT 2 — Part 5 correspondingly short; outcomes and substance use self-reported, some may be jokes (META_OFF_TOPIC_JOKE 5); the app was not installed. Bands (verbatim): " + table("## 1.5 Signal thresholds", 0) + " — at n=614 one review is 0.16%, seven 1.14% (Meaningful), 31 5.05% (High-priority); two findings promoted below their label on safety grounds: gambling ads (2) and data loss (3).", "n/a", "mixed", "614/614 read; 79 codes; 101 checks; 26 absence tests; low-info 281 (45.77%); ru 516", "none", "method", "generalisable", ["9568198570"], "", "")

c(3, "Warning 1; Warning 5; §6.7", "data-caveat", "Text reviewers are less positive than the public rating and one week explains most of the gap: 14,806 public ratings across the same 37 storefronts average 4.913★ vs corpus 4.397★ (+0.515★); before the July 2026 crash week the 515 reviews average 4.647★; one week (2026-07-16 → 07-22) holds 69 reviews (11.24%) and 40 of the 62 one- and two-star reviews — §9.D re-runs every headline without it.", "n/a", "mixed", "gap +0.515★ (pre-crash +0.27★); crash week 69 reviews / 40 of 62 low-star", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["14309392133"], "", "")

c(4, "§0.1; §0.1 table (verbatim)", "feature", "People value a simple, free counter that makes breaking a streak feel costly: U:praise_any 476 (77.52%, CI 74.1–80.6%, 4.81★), U:praise_specific 285 (46.42%) (verbatim): " + table("## 0.1 People value a simple", 0) + " — the mechanism is the number itself: 'breaking big numbers hurts far more than the urge to smoke' (ru, 4★); 'one reason not to relapse was that all the days would reset' (by, a month without cigarettes); 'seeing the numbers clearly calms me more than a pile of praise'; minimalism is a feature for this audience — 'the interface doesn't trigger — important for people with addictions, where an extra detail can set you off'; counter, reset and a diary-like comment 'to analyse a slip. Nothing else is needed'; free with many habits at once is what switchers name — 'the only free app so far that allows this without a subscription' (de); 'not forcing ads or payments like every other app, only free one out there' (us).", "counter to the second + reset + relapse note; nothing else", "praise", "praise_any 476 / 77.52% / 4.81★; SIMPLE_EASY 132 / 21.50%; outcome_any 118 / 19.22%; tracking_core 72; free_or_ads 43; DESIGN 39; GENERIC 184", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["10508150052", "13053806270", "13322337199", "12476493945", "13110607514", "10584087680", "12157232469"], "", "the loss-aversion of a big number is the retention mechanic — the app needs no gamification beyond the count")

c(5, "§0.2", "must-never-break", "In July 2026 one update made the app unusable for a week: BUG_CRASH 65 (10.59%, CI 8.4–13.3%, 2.23★), 64 of them in the seven days 2026-07-16 → 07-22 (the only other crash report is 2024-09); the week held 69 reviews, 64 crash reports, mean 2.41★, 40 of the corpus's 62 one- and two-star reviews; the day after release 1.2.0 (2026-07-15, 'translated into more languages') the first report arrived — 'after the last update the app crashes as soon as you open it'; BUG_AFTER_UPDATE 21 (3.42%); reviewers tie it to the new ad banner — BUG_CRASH_AD_LOAD 14 (2.28%): 'After recent update the app constantly crashes after the advertisement screen tries to load!'; 'the ad tries to load as soon as I open the app, and it crashes at once'; offline it works ('airplane mode helps'; 'with the internet off it runs stably'); the cost was records and users — 'I had lots of statistics and notes there; apparently I've lost it all'; 'if a relapse happens I won't be able to log it'; 'had to switch to a competitor'; fixed quickly — 1.2.1 shipped 2026-07-21 and on 07-22 a reviewer posted 'the crash bug was fixed'; the 30 reviews after 07-22 contain no crash report and average 4.70★; the same crash hit the developer's habit app ('the same happens with this developer's good-habits app').", "ad SDK load on launch crashes the app when online", "1★-burst", "BUG_CRASH 65 / 10.59% / 2.23★ (64 in one week); AFTER_UPDATE 21; CRASH_AD_LOAD 14; post-fix 30 reviews 4.70★ 0 crashes", "must-never-break", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["14309392133", "14317429024", "14321270649", "14316886107", "14317948166", "14313036902", "14331606843", "14332778196", "14334098154", "14317387419", "11735356386"], "", "a six-day fix ended the wave completely — the 1★ cost was bounded by the fix speed, not the bug")

c(6, "§0.3", "feature", "A widget is the single most requested thing in every year: REQ_WIDGET 86 (14.01%, CI 11.5–17.0%, 4.53★) — first 2023-02-06, last 2026-08-25; 19.3% of E1 reviews and still 14.4% of E3; it decides the fourth or fifth star — 30 of the 87 four-star reviews (34%) ask for one ('but the app has no widget', 4★; 'without a widget the app is pointless', 3★; 'no home-screen widgets … deleting', kz 4★); the reason is visibility, which is the product's whole mechanism — 'without one you can forget the app is even installed'; 'missing a lock-screen widget with the counter' (32 votes); one paying intent is conditional on it — 'ready to buy a subscription, but please add widgets' (5★); one reviewer claims the iPad has a widget, unverified.", "no widget at all", "request", "REQ_WIDGET 86 / 14.01% / 4.53★; 4★ share 34%; E1 19.3% → E3 14.4%; 32-vote review", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["9590848342", "14469862599", "12636973228", "13612784119", "14103004927", "12248437252", "10929591148", "10456809560", "11602446340"], "", "for a counter whose mechanism is seeing the number, a widget is the product on the home screen")

c(7, "§0.4", "feature", "Users want the counter to show progress, not only count it: U:motivation_layer_request 49 (7.98%, 4.35★) — tree growth, milestone notifications, quotes and achievements, colours; REQ_TREE_GROWTH 28 (4.56%, CI 3.2–6.5%), 27 from the RU storefront; the corpus's most-voted review (109 votes): 'why not add tree growth?'; 'the tree doesn't change, only the circle slowly closes … it doesn't motivate me much' (12 votes); by 2025 impatient — 'in all these years the developers haven't managed to add tree growth' (2★); goals — U:goal_setting 25 (4.07%): GOAL_STEPS_RIGID 15 ('after 7 days straight to 30'; sober 13 years against a 100-year goal: 'if I've been sober 13 years it makes more sense to aim for 15'), GOAL_HOWTO_QUESTION 13, and one says custom goals used to work ('I can't set custom goal times any more just is always 1 day', gb 3★); notifications — REQ_NOTIFICATIONS 11 (1.79%): 'no daily motivation, notifications or congratulations … after three days I forgot it existed' (2★).", "static tree logo; auto-stepping goal ladder; no notifications", "request", "motivation_layer 49 / 7.98%; TREE_GROWTH 28 / 4.56% (ru 27; 109 votes); goal_setting 25; STEPS_RIGID 15; HOWTO 13; NOTIFICATIONS 11", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["10801415396", "10450985364", "12966085325", "10814511549", "13804456581", "13034811450", "13305706545"], "", "a visual that implies growth and never grows reads as a broken promise")

c(8, "§0.5", "audience", "For a meaningful minority this is a recovery tool for self-harm and drugs: U:safety_sensitive 23 (3.75%, CI 2.5–5.6%, 4.96★) — USE_SELF_HARM 13 (2.12%), USE_DRUGS 8 (1.30%), USE_TREATMENT_CONTEXT 3; 'with this app I haven't harmed myself for a month'; self-harming for a year — 'this app really helps me hold back' (kz); 'held on almost a week, tracking in the app, but couldn't' (us); 'stopped snorting cocaine' (by, 7 votes); 'two rehabs didn't help'; a relapse log kept for a psychiatrist ('it's easier for my psychiatrist'); the listing describes smoking, alcohol, gambling and nail-biting and does not mention self-harm — 'the app is already used for self-harm recovery by reviewers who are likely young; its content, relapse copy and any ads shown to them are a safety question'.", "n/a", "praise", "safety_sensitive 23 / 3.75% / 4.96★; SELF_HARM 13; DRUGS 8; TREATMENT 3", "must-have", "Very strong", "generalisable", ["13609431141", "14176251516", "13807541941", "12210270920", "13783188576", "14057707333"], "", "")

c(9, "§0.6", "anti-pattern", "The free, ad-light app that reviewers praised is now criticised for its ads: before June 2024 no review complains about ads and PRAISE_NO_FEW_ADS 19 (3.09%) starts on day one ('great that there are no ads', 2023-01-31); U:ads_negative 20 (3.26%, 2.65★) from 2024-06-12 to 2026-06-20 — '15 mandatory seconds of ads every time you use the app' (co, 2★); ads every two minutes and 'to close it you have to exit completely' (1★); 6 of the 20 deleted the app; gambling ads inside an addiction app — ADS_HARMFUL_CONTENT 2 (promoted on safety grounds): 'it advertises betting and casinos to them … why not add alcohol and cigarette ads too?' (3★); 'ads for gambling, one of the addictions' (1★, titled 'scam'); in July 2026 the ad banner is what reviewers blame for the crash.", "interstitial ads on open; gambling ad category served in an addiction app", "complaint", "NO_FEW_ADS praise 19 (from day one); ads_negative 20 / 3.26% / 2.65★ (from 2024-06); deleted 6; HARMFUL_CONTENT 2", "must-never-break", "Very strong", "generalisable", ["9568198570", "11374484206", "13116009951", "12635810456", "13174041563"], "", "")

c(10, "§0.7", "monetization", "Monetisation barely registers: the only purchase is ad removal (Monthly $0.99 / Yearly $9.99; RU 99 ₽ / 699 ₽); PAID_EXPLICIT 2 (0.33%), both for ad removal and both satisfied ('paid at once — you can't start a tracker like this by watching smelly ads'; 'Well the were ads before I paid for them'); six Russian reviewers believe the app is paid — PAYWALL_PERCEIVED 6 (0.98%), all RU ('you can't even see the interface; a fully paid app', 1★; 'nothing but ads, and everything only for a month', 1★); subscription format, not price, is the objection — 'sad you can't switch ads off for life' (kz, 3★); 'you should add a lifetime purchase; I want to buy' (vn, 5★).", "ad-removal subscription only; no lifetime", "purchase-driver", "PAID 2 / 0.33%; PAYWALL_PERCEIVED 6 / 0.98% (all ru); WANT_ONE_TIME 2", "product-rule", "Emerging", "generalisable", ["11651806786", "13254705653", "11890941612", "13029179785", "14162589436", "11641762030"], "", "")

c(11, "§0.8", "data-caveat", "What is absent across 614 reviews (26 multilingual patterns, every hit read): no Android comparison, no privacy or tracking concern although the listing declares 'Data Used to Track You', no mention of a developer reply or support contact, no AI request; backup or transfer to a new phone raised 4 times (REQ_BACKUP_SYNC 4, 0.65%); only one price quoted by a reviewer (100₽).", "n/a", "mixed", "privacy 0; support mention 0; AI 0; BACKUP_SYNC 4; price quotes 1", "none", "Weak", "generalisable", ["12839988426"], "", "")

c(12, "§2.3 table (verbatim); §2.3; §2.4 table (verbatim); §2.4", "monetization", "Free / paid / trial / unclear (verbatim): " + table("## 2.3 Free / paid / trial", 0) + " — counter, unlimited habits, records, relapse notes and articles are free (PRAISE_FREE 30: 'for being able to use all functions without payment'); removing ads is a monthly or yearly subscription; lifetime ad removal not offered (WANT_ONE_TIME_PURCHASE 2); goal duration unclear — one asks if it is paid-only, others say it cannot be set; trial unclear — one reviewer describes a 'free trial for a month' that still tried to charge after cancelling (TRIAL_USER 1), the listing shows no trial; perceived as paid — belief, not listing (6 RU). Data and privacy (verbatim): " + table("## 2.4 Data and privacy statements", 0) + " — no reviewer raises privacy, tracking or data use, yet reviewers name what they track — self-harm, cocaine, injected drugs, masturbation — in an app whose label declares tracking for advertising (location, identifiers, usage, diagnostics); four ask how to keep their data on a new phone and one fears losing 'lots of statistics and notes' in the crash.", "free core; ads tracking label beside sensitive use", "mixed", "PRAISE_FREE 30; WANT_ONE_TIME 2; TRIAL_USER 1; PAYWALL_PERCEIVED 6; privacy concern 0; BACKUP_SYNC 4", "none", "table", "generalisable", ["11687074576", "11641762030", "14162589436", "10306903519", "13524890756", "12839988426", "14510416958", "14313036902"], "", "")

